  isFinal: 0
  edition: "Baku  \xB7  Thursday edition  \xB7  Vol. XII, No. 203"
  flavorHeadlines:
  - Carpet Museum Extends Evening Hours
  - Taxi Fares to Rise Ahead of Festival Season
  - Local Chess Club Takes Regional Title
  leadHeadline: Widow's Flat on Lantern Lane Empty Since Spring. Neighbours Still
    Hear the Table Being Set
  leadDetail: Heard every evening around 7 PM, Lantern Lane No. 6.
  leadReaction:
  - speaker: Dutch
    text: Lantern Lane. Dinner for one at seven, every night. Sure.
  arrivalLines:
  - speaker: Dutch
    text: Lantern Lane, number six, third floor. Dining room's been dusted. By who?
  bookRevealLines: []
  identifyLines:
  - speaker: Dutch
    text: The Echo. Not a ghost. A habit with nobody left to have it.
  - speaker: Dutch
    text: It's bound to something it lost. The silver on the table, then.
  wrongToolLine: I try the {0}. The whisper doesn't even pause.
  resolveLines:
  - speaker: Dutch
    text: The spoon goes back in its slot. Twelve of twelve.
  - speaker: 
    text: The whispering stops mid-word. The table is set. Nobody comes to eat.
  - speaker: Dutch
    text: Dinner's served, Mrs. A.
